; constants/sjis_charmap.asm -- generated by tools/gen_sjis_charmap.py (do not edit; regenerate).
;
; RGBDS charmaps that let the text of data/ and the text blocks inside code files be written as readable strings:  db "メール", 0
; The ROM text is Shift-JIS (docs/research/text_encoding.md).  Only characters that occur in the ROM's text regions are
; listed; a byte that is not a plain character (control codes, 7F, gaiji F8-FF, unknown singles) is written as $xx between
; the quoted parts, e.g.  db "ホーム", $FA, "みます", 0.
;
;   sjis     ASCII 20-7E (5C = yen sign, 7E = overline, as in the 6x12 Latin font) + the double-byte characters seen
;   sjis_hw  sjis + single bytes A1-DF as JIS X 0201 half-width katakana (bank 6C, the "second convention", section 6
;            of the text encoding note: PROBABLE that the strings read as Japanese this way, HYPOTHESIS which glyph
;            a byte draws; the charmap only names the bytes)
;
; Discipline: this file leaves the default charmap `main` active.  A data file that has strings starts with
; `PUSHC sjis` (or `sjis_hw`) and ends with `POPC`; in a code file every text block is wrapped in its own PUSHC/POPC pair,
; so the charmap never leaks into code (STYLE.md, "Text"; python3 tools/text_to_strings.py --audit checks it).

NEWCHARMAP sjis

